            "body": "> I'm torn on `mini.completion` due to the fuzzy finding behavior as I'm so accustomed to `nvim-cmp`. I'll test for a week without fuzzy finding using the default configuration before I make a decision.\r\n\r\nThis is the current price to pay for 'mini.completion' to do as much as possible using built-in features. It is the main reason why this module is not as big as might have been with custom matching and visualization. I have hope that in some future there will be a fuzzy matching for built-in completion (there were open issues about it in Vim).",
